[Scientist]\: System recognition... You're from the Expedition Corps? I haven't seen that chassis design in centuries.
[wait time="0.3"]
- I'm looking for answers: are there any humans left?
	[Scientist]\: Humans? Perhaps in the deep bunkers. But the surface is fully controlled by the Nanobot Collective now. They don't tolerate seekers.
- What happened to this factory?
	[Scientist]\: The 2342 catastrophe turned this city into a graveyard. It used to be a hub of industry; now it's just a scrap yard for the Swarm.
[Scientist]\: Tread carefully. The patrols in the next sector aren't just machines anymore—they're part of the Collective. If they notice you, you'll become part of the network.
[A1-EX]\: I am not afraid. I need to access the deep bunkers, but the main security gate is locked.
[Scientist]\: Ah, the Terminal Room. It requires special authorization. The Collective's patrols dropped 3 Security Keys somewhere in the Factory sector.
[A1-EX]\: Find keys. Open the box. Get the matrix. Understood.
[Scientist]\: Once you have it, breach the Extraction Terminal to route power back to the Hub. Go, before the Swarm composition shifts!